>> s.a = 1;
>> s.b = 'text';
>> s.c = [1 2 3];
>> s.d = {1, 'two'};
>> s.e.inner = 5;
>> s
s =
  struct with fields:

    a: 1
    b: 'text'
    c: [1 2 3]
    d: {1x2 cell}
    e: [1x1 struct]
>> t = struct('x', {1, 2})
t =
  1x2 struct array with fields:

    x
>> t(2)
ans =
  struct with fields:

    x: 2
>> u = struct('m', magic(3))
u =
  struct with fields:

    m: [3x3 double]
>> v = struct('e', {})
v =
  0x0 empty struct array with fields:

    e
>> w.f = @(x) x + 1;
>> w
w =
  struct with fields:

    f: @(x)x+1
